---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const stack = ['Feature scoring', 'Accuracy verification', 'Field intelligence'];
---

<Base
  title="Competitive Intelligence Matrix Case Study | Ishraq Alam"
  description="A living, accuracy-verified comparison of Nourish against 9+ care-sector competitors with a field-intelligence layer."
>
  <article>
    <section class="cs-hero">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <a href="/case-studies/" class="back">← All case studies</a>
        <span class="eyebrow">Case study · Living document</span>
        <h1>Competitive Intelligence Matrix</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          A living comparison of Nourish against 9+ care-sector competitors, including
          Roundsys, Birdie, Unique IQ, and PCS, built so every conversation about a
          competitor starts from verified facts, not folklore.
        </p>
        <ul class="chips">
          {stack.map((item) => <li class="chip chip-blue">{item}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pb-0">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
        <h2>Two layers: verified truth and field signal</h2>
        <p>
          The core is an accuracy-verified feature scoring matrix. Every claim about a
          competitor's product is checked before it goes in, so reps never repeat a
          myth to a prospect who knows better.
        </p>
        <p>
          On top sits a <strong>"Field Intelligence"</strong> layer: unverified feedback
          heard from prospects in live conversations. It's kept deliberately separate
          and labelled as signal, not fact, so the matrix captures what the market is
          saying without contaminating what we know to be true.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="container narrow">
        <span class="eyebrow">Why it matters</span>
        <h2>Competitive knowledge that compounds</h2>
        <p>
          Most competitive intel lives in Slack threads and dies there. A living matrix
          means every prospect conversation makes the whole team sharper. It's the same
          system-building instinct behind the CQC dashboard, applied to knowledge
          instead of data.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a href="/case-studies/cqc-dashboard/" class="btn btn-ghost">Back to: CQC Research Dashboard →</a>
          <a href="/enterprise/" class="btn btn-primary">Work with me</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>

  <style>
    .cs-hero { padding-top: 80px; padding-bottom: 0; }

    .back {
      display: inline-block;
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }

    .pb-0 { padding-bottom: 0; }

    .cta-row {
      display: flex;
      gap: 14px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      margin-top: 28px;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
